{"title":"Career Roadmap · Cardiac Technician","role":"Cardiac Technician","summary":"A Cardiac Technician supports the diagnosis, monitoring, testing, and treatment of patients with cardiovascular conditions. The role combines cardiac diagnostic technology, patient monitoring, ECG, cardiovascular testing, emergency support, equipment handling, and clinical documentation.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Cardiac Care / Cardiovascular Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Cardiac Technician supports the diagnosis, monitoring, testing, and treatment of patients with cardiovascular conditions. The role combines cardiac diagnostic technology, patient monitoring, ECG, cardiovascular testing, emergency support, equipment handling, and clinical documentation."},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on specialization and employer, cardiac technicians may work in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cardiology departments"},{"text":"Cardiac diagnostic units"},{"text":"Cardiac catheterization laboratories"},{"text":"Cardiac intensive care units"},{"text":"Non-invasive cardiology laboratories"},{"text":"Cardiac rehabilitation services"},{"text":"Hospitals and specialty cardiac centres"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Common technical areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ECG"},{"text":"Holter monitoring"},{"text":"Exercise stress testing"},{"text":"Echocardiography support, where appropriately trained"},{"text":"Cardiac monitoring"},{"text":"Cath-lab support"},{"text":"Pacemaker/device-related procedures"},{"text":"Emergency cardiac care support"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact duties depend on the qualification, institutional role, supervision, and applicable professional requirements."}]},{"heading":"Recommended Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Cardiac Care / Cardiovascular Technology Degre